{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"f330792f5fa9393a","name":"card_unit_738_jager_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/CovertOp/units/card_unit_738_jager_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"738. JÄGER REGIMENT","text":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDraw a card when it is destroyed.","flavorText":"The German Jäger divisions were light divisions specially trained for combat in difficult terrain. They were smaller than the standard infantry divisions, and more heavily armed than mountain divisions, but not as much as larger infantry formations, especially when it came to artillery support. The 738th Jäger Regiment was a unit of the 118th Jäger Division of the German Wehrmacth. The division was formed in 1941 as the 718th Infantry Division, and redesignated 118th Jäger Division in 1943. In 1941 the division was transferred to Yugoslavia and was mainly assigned to anti-partisan and internal security operations. In 1943 it participated in the Battle of the Sutjeska against the Yugoslav Partisan force and later saw fighting again in Bosnia and Croatia. During the final stages of the war it fought against the Soviet Red Army in the Vienna offensive, before retreating and surrendering to the British in May 1945.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_738_jager_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_738_jager_regiment_title","SourceString":"738. JÄGER REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"738. JÄGER REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":1,"defense":2,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_738_jager_regiment_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDraw a card when it is destroyed.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDraw a card when it is destroyed."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_738_jager_regiment_history","SourceString":"The German Jäger divisions were light divisions specially trained for combat in difficult terrain. They were smaller than the standard infantry divisions, and more heavily armed than mountain divisions, but not as much as larger infantry formations, especially when it came to artillery support. The 738th Jäger Regiment was a unit of the 118th Jäger Division of the German Wehrmacth. The division was formed in 1941 as the 718th Infantry Division, and redesignated 118th Jäger Division in 1943. In 1941 the division was transferred to Yugoslavia and was mainly assigned to anti-partisan and internal security operations. In 1943 it participated in the Battle of the Sutjeska against the Yugoslav Partisan force and later saw fighting again in Bosnia and Croatia. During the final stages of the war it fought against the Soviet Red Army in the Vienna offensive, before retreating and surrendering to the British in May 1945.","LocalizedString":"The German Jäger divisions were light divisions specially trained for combat in difficult terrain. They were smaller than the standard infantry divisions, and more heavily armed than mountain divisions, but not as much as larger infantry formations, especially when it came to artillery support. The 738th Jäger Regiment was a unit of the 118th Jäger Division of the German Wehrmacth. The division was formed in 1941 as the 718th Infantry Division, and redesignated 118th Jäger Division in 1943. In 1941 the division was transferred to Yugoslavia and was mainly assigned to anti-partisan and internal security operations. In 1943 it participated in the Battle of the Sutjeska against the Yugoslav Partisan force and later saw fighting again in Bosnia and Croatia. During the final stages of the war it fought against the Soviet Red Army in the Vienna offensive, before retreating and surrendering to the British in May 1945."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTa